{#
  The one confirmation for an irreversible action: a service's own DeploymentAction
  (sleep, wake) and the dangerous project actions (delete a project, deployment,
  component or attachment, reprocess).

  Expects: action (DeploymentAction or ProjectAction), key, message. Optional:
  blocked_reason. The endpoint comes from the action itself, server-side; this template
  never sees a URL from the request.

  Nothing here is shown. openConfirmAction() in static/js/edit_modal.js puts this fragment
  in the still-closed shared modal, asks the question in the page's confirmation dialog
  (bg/_bevestiging.html.j2), and opens the modal only after "yes", with the progress. The
  question used to live in the modal itself, which then jumped from wide to narrow and
  back.

  The CSRF header sits on the WRAPPER, not on the element with hx-post: htmx inherits it
  from an ancestor. The JS only starts the POST (htmx.trigger "confirmed") and never reads
  the token.
#}
<div data-confirm-action="{{ key }}"
     data-question="{{ blocked_reason or message }}"
     data-button="{{ action.label }}"
     {% if action.kind in ('warning', 'warning-subtle') %}data-destructive{% endif %}
     hx-headers='{"X-CSRF-Token": "{{ request.state.csrf_token }}"}'>
    {# A blocked action has nothing to confirm: no POST, only the explanation (the server
       refuses it as well). #}
    {% if not blocked_reason %}
    <div class="confirm-action-submit"
         hx-post="{{ action.endpoint }}"
         hx-trigger="confirmed"
         hx-target="#edit-section-inner"
         hx-swap="innerHTML"></div>
    {% endif %}
    <div class="edit-section-loading">
        <c-paragraph>Starten...</c-paragraph>
    </div>

    {# Where the modal shell writes the error when the POST fails. #}
    <div id="confirm-action-error" class="edit-section-error is-hidden"></div>
</div>
